<title>FINLAND: UPM TO BUY PEAT FOR FIM 250 MLN - VAPO.</title>
<headline>UPM TO BUY PEAT FOR FIM 250 MLN - VAPO.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish state-owned peat producer Vapo said in a statement on Monday it had won a 250 million markka five-year order for energy peat from Finnish forest industry group UPM-Kymmene.</p>
<p>&quot;Vapo will deliver to UPM-Kymmene's mills' power plants energy peat for a value of 50 million markka annually in the period 1998-2002,&quot; Vapo said.</p>
<p>In Finland, UPM uses some 26 terawatt hours a year of heat energy, of which over 10 percent is produced from peat, it said.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki Newsroom +358-9-680 50 242, news@reuters.fi</p>
